        <!-- =============================================================
             2. TAB: ORAIN FORGE
             ============================================================= -->
        <div id="orain-forge" class="tab-panel">
            <section class="section-block reveal">
                <div class="container">
                    <span class="label-sm">CONSTRUCTION LAYER &bull; KERNEL TECHNOLOGY</span>
                    <h1 class="headline-xl">ORAIN Forge</h1>
                    <p class="body-lg">
                        The geometry construction and execution technology behind ORAIN. Forge is designed to transform structured geometric instructions into precise, engineering-grade CAD geometry through robust computational geometry and CAD-kernel technology.
                    </p>

                    <div class="statement-card" style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
                        <span class="label-sm">CORE MANDATE</span>
                        <h2 class="headline-md">From Geometric Intent to Physical Geometry</h2>
                        <p class="body-lg">
                            Generating engineering geometry is fundamentally different from generating a visual approximation. A usable engineering model must maintain precise dimensions, topology, relationships, and geometric integrity. Forge sits at the point where geometric intelligence becomes physical geometry.
                        </p>
                        <div class="tag-footer" style="font-size: 0.85rem;">
                            Geometric Plan &rarr; CAD Operations &rarr; B-Rep Geometry &rarr; Engineering Output
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="cards-grid-2">
                        <div class="product-card">
                            <div>
                                <span class="badge-mono">ENGINEERING RIGOR</span>
                                <h3 class="headline-sm">Built for Engineering Geometry</h3>
                                <p class="body-md">
                                    Forge provides the computational foundation required to construct what the system has reasoned and planned:
                                </p>
                                <ul class="spec-list">
                                    <li>Precise geometric construction</li>
                                    <li>Feature and operation execution</li>
                                    <li>Topological consistency &amp; manifold integrity</li>
